# A minimal template for a Tau REPL demo script.
#
# See demos/README.md for how to run this script, and for the conventions the
# other demos follow.

# Lines starting with # are comments. They are passed to the REPL, which ignores
# them, so they appear in the transcript as the demo runs. A line containing a
# doubled hash is dropped by run.sh instead, which is how to leave a note meant
# for the reader of the script rather than for the transcript. This line is one:
## you will not see this line when the demo runs.

# Any REPL command can go in a script. `help` lists them all, and
# `help <command>` explains one:

version

# Remember that a blank line is skipped rather than sent, so a run waiting at its
# `continue? [Enter]/[q]:` prompt has to be advanced by a non-empty line -- the
# demos use a `# step` comment for that. See demo_3.1-interpreter_sbf.tau.

# End the script with quit, so the REPL exits instead of waiting for more input.

quit
